An identity conversion (var _ T = an expression already of type T) consumes and
produces the same type. Rather than surfacing later as a self-referential
dependency cycle, it is rejected as an invalid (no-op) conversion at discovery,
naming the real cause.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrInvalidConversion
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type MyInt int

//plumb:build
var _ MyInt = 5

//plumb:build
func Use(m MyInt) string { return "" }
